  "purpose": "Translate the owner's 'from A to Z' requirement into a durable whole-game completeness contract. The project team owns discovery of missing details; the owner is not expected to enumerate every bird, bark, door, animation, sound, interaction or failure case.",
  "definition_of_complete": "A game area/system is complete only when all applicable domains below are explicitly satisfied or marked N_A with rationale, and the required evidence gates are met. Silence in the plan is never interpreted as 'not needed'.",
  "global_rules": [
    "No hidden omission: every applicable domain must have an explicit status.",
    "No partial-import completion: a partially populated bank or partially implemented system cannot be labeled complete.",
    "No evidence inflation: planning, source discovery, generated media, compile success, PIE, device and human acceptance are separate states.",
    "Prepare future-needed assets/data/contracts early when that preparation is offline-safe, even if runtime integration is gate-blocked.",
    "Do not build runtime features that violate active Governor gate ordering; preparation and sourcing may proceed on isolated branches.",
    "All heavy assets use soft references/async loading; no heavy synchronous LoadObject expansion.",
    "Crowd-scale NPCs use pooling/relevance throttling; repeated world detail uses ISM/HISM/culling.",
    "Animated production characters are skeletal FBX. OBJ character pieces remain prototype/foundation only.",
    "Production textures are PNG/TGA/channel-packed where appropriate; no BMP production texture path.",
    "All story/lore details remain source-grounded and original dialogue never copies Tolkien/movie lines verbatim.",
    "Every real code change updates CURRENT_PROJECT_STATE and PRODUCTION_COMPLETENESS_MATRIX in the same work unit."
  ],
